==Battleground==
*1 [[Masked Okame]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 29.33~32 seconds<sup>880f~960f</sup>.
*5 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 58.67~60 seconds<sup>1,760f~1,800f</sup>.
*3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 5.33~8 seconds<sup>160f~240f</sup>.
*3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>, delay 1~3.33 seconds<sup>30f~100f</sup>.
*3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 193.33 seconds<sup>5,800f</sup>, delay 3.33~6 seconds<sup>100f~180f</sup>.
*5 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 253.33 seconds<sup>7,600f</sup>, delay 6.67~9.33 seconds<sup>200f~280f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This endurance battle is all about stalling with burst damage until most of the peons stop spawning. With 100% Knockback on hit and Freeze Immunity, Masked Okame's relentless attacks can and will push through everything she hits. Short-ranged, slow attackers are not recommended for the boss, since her 800-range Omni Strike will easily beat them into submission.

There are 5 different waves of Gory Darks, each of which you must counter both quickly and effectively so you can go back to stalling Okame. Use [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] between peon waves to completely stop Okame from advancing.

As Okame does not flinch from damage until slain, [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper]] and Breakerblast should prove useful on this stage, as they'll be one of your only ways of regaining ground against her.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Crystal Li'l Gau Gau]]: Being an [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark]] Specialist Meatshield with [[Immune to Knockback|Knockback Immunity]], this unit can easily withstand several punishing attacks from Okame and other [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] threats. It won't hold up against Ginger Snaches, but there won't be many superior alternatives anywhere else.
*[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]]: Roe Cat's Resistance to, and [[Weaken]] ability against [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] makes it incredibly durable against its target trait despite being vulnerable to Knockback. It leaves Okame with no opportunity to push, though the Dark threats must be dealt with accordingly.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Boulder Cat's massive health and Knockback Immunity allows it to stall any enemy in this stage, and gets more consistent with Research [[Cat Combo|Combos]] while the other units catch up.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]/[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: Both units provide valuable [[Slow]] effects against non-[[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies at extreme range, with Cyberpunk's Long Distance attacks hitting everything in a small area while Sniper's single-target attacks knock back everything on hit. Both can't work alone, but definitely make things much easier.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Bullet Train is a very fast rusher with the Money Up ability and decent damage. Combined with Boulder, Bullet Train can pick off Doge Darks to ease any economical pressure. It has full backswing, as well as enough health to withstand one attack from Okame at level 40. Bullet Train has the potential to attack twice or more when dispatched, accumulating valuable chip damage over time on Okame.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]]: With Massive Damage, Attack Buff and Defense Buff Talents, Heavy Assault C.A.T. serves as a very competent attacker. As the unit's speed, area attack, and anti-Dark Weaken all help to remove such threats from play despite its high cost.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Assassin BearCat]]: Assassin BearCat is a disposable, somewhat fast melee attacker with [[Insane Damage]] against Dark, held back by incredibly low range. It is recommended to level him to 43 or above in order to tank a Gory Dark hit. Can be occasionally inconsistent against Doge Darks, but he still does a lot and can quickly nuke Dark peons with proper support.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: Pizza Cat is a midranger with [[Massive Damage]] against Darks, although unusable against Okame due to having very slow speed and low standing range. Pizza Cat is still an important inclusion as he can comfortably deal with those nasty Gory Darks, who will more often than not advance far beyond Okame's standing range and can be difficult to handle with their high health.
*[[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]]: Neo Cutter Cat works just as well as it did in [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]]. Having 100% chance to Survive a lethal strike, 400% Strengthen at 1% health and Massive Damage to Reds, this cheap unit can deal incredible bursts of damage to Okame should it attack successfully while Strengthened. While Ginger Snaches won't stand a chance, Cutter is hindered significantly by its long cooldown and Dark peons, so it must be used with caution.
*[[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]]: Manic Island Cat is an incredibly good general purpose unit, thanks to its low cost and good stats. Being [[Strong Against]] Reds as well, it can survive multiple Okame hits and deal incredibly high chip damage while consistently handling the Ginger Snache waves. Doesn't work so well when the Dark enemies arrive, but it still provides great value for what it does.
*[[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]]: While more expensive than and not as strong as its Manic counterpart, normal Island is still a solid choice for wearing down Okame and dispatching the Ginger Snaches. Additionally, when paired with [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Fisherman Cat]] and the above-mentioned Manic Island, the player gets two solid [[Cat Combo]]s in one: [[Cap'n Ahab (Combo)|Cap'n Ahab]] and [[Moby Dick (Combo)|Moby Dick]].
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Bahamut doesn't do very well on the stage, and won't get to deal much damage due to having terrible health and low range. However, his very high speed and powerful area attacks can be useful in a pinch against Gory Darks, or to help with cleanup once Okame's support runs dry. The [[Explosion]] [[Talents|Talent]] is highly recommended, as it increases his damage output greatly.
*[[Rei Ayanami (???) (Super Rare Cat)|Rei Ayanami (???)]]: Though she is a collab unit, making her slightly difficult to access, she has Resistance and a chance to Weaken Dark enemies plus immunity to Knockback, making her excellent on this stage as she is basically the anti-Dark equivalent of Roe Cat. Do be aware that her Knockback Immunity will lead to Okame attacking more often, which can be very harmful combined with Okame's massive Omni range.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]: A rusher with short cooldown, low cost, high speed and Massive Damage to Darks, enabling aggressive use of him against Okame and most of the peons. Make sure you have a clear shot before sending him out, though.
*[[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Keiji]]: A decent midranged tank unit with [[Resistant]] to Darks and with a 100% strengthen at 50% health, he can deal some serious damage. He serves as a good wall for your frontline defense, especially against the annoying peons in the stage. Despite having more range, he'll have a hard time trying to hit Okame since he's vulnerable to Knockback.
*[[Urashima Taro (Uber Rare Cat)|King Gamereon]]: Gamereon is a midranged tanker who boasts extreme health against Dark enemies and has enough damage to easily kill the peons. However, as with Keiji, Gameron is vulnerable to knockback and can be pushed away easily. Combined with his slow attacks, Gameron won't work alone either.
*[[Musashi Miyamoto (Legend Rare Cat)|Musashi Miyamoto]]: Due to his devastating anti-Dark offense and defense, Musashi Miyamoto can almost solo the entire stage. Make sure you also have something to take out the Ginger Snaches, and you can win with nearly zero effort by spawning him and watching the destruction unfold.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]]: Similar to Miyamoto, his high anti-Traited DPS makes him incredibly devastating towards Okame and the Gory Darks. Because of his Multi-Hit, if Okame attacks him before he lands his third attack, he'll be able to immediately retaliate, dealing even more damage. His conjure is also useful for gaining ground and getting more chain-hits in. Unlike Miyamoto, he lacks the Resistant ability to last longer and has a lower standing range, but can snipe Okame if there are peons to be used as stepping stones.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]]: Jizo's first form is a disposable midranger with Massive Damage against Dark. He won't be able to deal with Okame, but is instead useful in neutralizing Gory Darks and Doge Darks.
*Talented [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]]: With the Immune to Knockback talent, Cat Machine Mk 3 can completely wall Okame. Its extremely high health vs. Red and solid attack power make it a very good choice, provided you want to spend the not-insignificant 100 NP required. Support, however, is needed to deal with the Gory Dark waves, because they will shred it if left alone.
*[[Mighty Sphinx Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Hyper Battalion Convoys]]: Battalion is a frontline tank and a very reliable unit, specifically in [[True Form]], because of its Knockback and 100% chance to generate [[Wave Attack]]s. Okame's 100% chance of Knockback will just cause Battalion to rebound, pushing Okame further to the base and deal extra chip damage. You just need to protect it against the Dark peons.

